# VVDN -- COORDINATED 35L/35R OPS, 2 ARR + 2 DEP (per user spec, reworded 2026-08-06).
# Arrivals VDN651/652 appear at DOTEN, ILS Y 35L, 3-min separation.
# Departures VDN751/752 push back from real Gate 36 (apt.dat), 35R, 2min30s separation.
# All coordinates real, most reused verbatim (live-tested this session) from
# VVDN_35L35R_COORDINATED_OPS.scn: DOTEN/STAR/ILS35L track, G4/G6 exit-hold points, Gate 26/11,
# pre-hold node41 "A_stop", and DEP_HOLD (the real RWY 35R threshold-area lineup point).
#
# Both DEP1 and DEP2 line up at the SAME DEP_HOLD=(16.0292,108.2025) heading 352, sequentially
# (per the user's explicit spec -- an earlier draft used two slightly different lineup points,
# corrected here). Both fly a real BUNTA 2G SID (RWY 35) after an initial straight RWY_HDG climb
# to 1500ft (standard "climb runway heading to altitude, then turn" SID technique -- needed
# because the real BUNTA 2G "CF DN456" leg's course does not originate at the runway itself in
# the AIXM data; the runway-heading segment also keeps the crossing-reference points below
# reliably on-path).
#
# The two pairs use DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT crossing-clearance triggers, matching the user's own
# differently-worded spec for each:
#  - Pair 1: ARR1 may cross 35R only once DEP1 has itself passed G4_PT=(16.0489,108.1987) -- the
#    SAME coordinate ARR1 holds short of. Verified this session: G4_PT sits ~101.6m cross-track
#    off DEP1's straight climb-out line, ~207m along-track past liftoff, so the live ATDIST check
#    (registered on DEP1, targeting G4_PT) uses a 150m/0.081NM radius, not the tight ~37m used
#    elsewhere -- confirmed necessary and sufficient by this session's Explore-agent geometry pass.
#  - Pair 2: ARR2 may cross only once DEP2 has flown the WHOLE of RWY 35R (a stronger, later
#    condition) -- live ATDIST on 16.0574,108.1984 (near the real far/17L threshold), unchanged
#    from the original 3-pair file.
#
# Gate 26 (ARR1's parking) and Gate 11 (ARR2's parking) are not both specified in the user's
# request -- ARR2's stand was explicitly left to my choice; both are real,
# taxiway-connected apt.dat parkings already used/verified in the prior scenario
# (16.05262199,108.2019728 and 16.0578,108.2014 respectively).
#
# SEQUENCE per user spec:
#  1. ARR1 (VDN651) lands 35L; 30s after gear touchdown (ATALT 0 DELAY 30), DEP1 (VDN751,
#     already holding at DEP_HOLD) begins its takeoff roll (real BADA B738 performance) then
#     flies the real SID. The INSTANT DEP1 starts rolling, DEP2 (VDN752, staged since pushback
#     at PRE_HOLD/node41) is released onto the runway to line up at the SAME DEP_HOLD, heading 352.
#     ARR1 exits 35L via G4, holding before G4_PT -- may not taxi past it toward 35R until DEP1
#     has itself passed G4_PT (live ATDIST, see above). Then ARR1 crosses 35R and taxis to
#     Gate 26, DEL 10s after arrival.
#  2. 30s after ARR2 (VDN652) gear touchdown, DEP2 begins its takeoff roll + real SID climb.
#     ARR2 exits 35L via G6 (16.0572,108.1974) and holds. Once DEP2 has flown the whole of
#     RWY 35R (live ATDIST on 16.0574,108.1984), ARR2 crosses and taxis to Gate 11, DEL 10s
#     after arrival.
00:00:00.00>TRAILS ON
00:00:00.00>ASAS OFF

